---
description: Branch from fresh main before feature work or PRs — prevents duplicate cherry-pick PRs (#58/#59/#60).
alwaysApply: true
---

# Git branches — fresh base required

Before creating a branch or opening a PR:

1. `git fetch origin`
2. `git checkout main && git pull --ff-only origin main`
3. `git checkout -b feat/<short-name>` from updated `main`
4. Run `npm run check:branch-fresh` before `gh pr create`

Do **not** open a second PR for the same work if one already exists — update the existing branch instead.

If CI fails with a stale merge base, merge `origin/main` into the branch (do not blindly cherry-pick and re-open).

Never append Cursor attribution trailers to commits (see git-commits rule).
